  "description": "Bootstrap from hosted pytest duration reports. Unlisted phases conservatively use the smallest listed duration (the top-N report cutoff). Structured future reports include every phase. Entries the CIROOT2 change made cheaper (validator link cache, lean validation links) were re-measured on 2026-10-28 on a matched 2-core local run (taskset, GOMAXPROCS=2, race, GOPROXY=off, cold per-test link cache) and recorded as 1.5x the measured seconds until a hosted run refreshes them with update_go_test_costs.py. Deferred tests were then re-measured together in one process with a shared link cache (matched 2-core local, race, -parallel=2; the way a CI bucket runs) and recorded as 1.25x the measured seconds. CICACHE3: newly classified memory-validator and link-wrapper fixture consumers measured locally on 2026-10-29 at 1e6c3b449 (2 pytest workers, GOMAXPROCS=4, shared prepared operator/compiler cache); new entries reserve 1.5x complete setup/call/teardown time pending hosted refresh. Existing hosted bounds are retained. The six RBAC/replay Go consumers caught by the fixture-wide guard were likewise measured serially (6 passed in 6.27s) and seeded at 1.5x their complete phases.",
